Didn't get the dump patch (I am too lazy) and the game took several
months with hiatus in between.  So my memory is sketchy as well.  Just
some thoughts.

I went with 'almost conductless'.  I never polyselfed, and I was going
to go geno-less to see more monsters, but since one of the throne gave
me a genocide, I geno-ed Disenchanters.  End game was pretty fun with
all the big monsters (I had a character-class monster with -33 AC
running around in the Astral Plane!  I shoulda checked the items on
that guy to see if there was anything fantastic...).

Wizards r0x0rs.  Especially post Quest.  With the amulet of 'I
regenerate my power points faster than than I can spend', I had Haste
Self on quasi-permanently (I coulda ditched the speed boots and went
with something like water walking or something while keeping the very
fast status), had Detect Monster on pretty much all the time (Although
I have to recast the spell about once in 40 turns), Magic Mapped,
detect food, and detect treasure all the levels.  Fireballs and Cone of
Ice comes in very handy at times (Freezing water and lava was fun).
Got up to lvl 30 and had all the spells with maxed out skill levels.
Some of the bonus of having higher skills like detect food, levitation,
Fireball and Cone of Ice, were fun.

Along with the power generation and spell selection, I also
puddng-farmed.  It went super fast with Extra Healing spell and mana
regeneration from the amulet.  I ended up with 3 Magic Lamps, Helm of
Brilliance (I was missing that so I was pleased), and almost 2 complete
sets of spell books.  Plus my final AC was -56, 700+ hps and 500+ Power
w/ 10 scrolls of charging for the final run.  I can see why this can be
